  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>What's on the Backyard Bacon Ranch Stackburger</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>100% real seasoned beef patty</strong> — Never frozen, cooked to order</li>
    <li><strong>Crispy bacon</strong> — Two strips, smoky and crisp</li>
    <li><strong>Cheddar cheese</strong> — Sharp cheddar, melted on the patty</li>
    <li><strong>Ranch sauce</strong> — Creamy, herby, generous amount</li>
    <li><strong>Crisp lettuce</strong> — Fresh, adds a cool crunch</li>
    <li><strong>Tomato</strong> — Sliced, balances the richness</li>
    <li><strong>Toasted bun</strong> — Holds up to the toppings</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Find this and all DQ burgers on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a> or browse the <a href="/categories/burgers-sandwiches">Burgers &amp; Sandwiches category</a>.</p>
  <h2>Backyard Bacon Ranch vs. FlameThrower Stackburger</h2>
  <p>These are DQ's two most popular Stackburgers. The choice between them is simple:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose <strong>Backyard Bacon Ranch</strong> ($9.99) if you want a bold, satisfying burger without heat. Classic bacon-ranch-cheddar profile, lower price.</li>
    <li>Choose <a href="/items/flamethrower-stackburger"><strong>FlameThrower® Stackburger</strong></a> ($10.87) if you want spice. Pepper Jack, jalapeños, and FlameThrower sauce create moderate-to-bold heat.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Best Value Pairing</h2>
  <p>The Backyard Bacon Ranch does not qualify for the <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> (which uses the Original Cheeseburger). But paired with <a href="/items/regular-fries">Regular Fries</a> ($2.49) and a <a href="/items/vanilla-soft-serve-cone">Vanilla Cone</a> ($2.39) for dessert, you get a complete meal for approximately $14.87.</p>
